From 63b1d57d1c8418855e07b36415e0738b920478d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:19:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 073/149] media: qcom: camss: Set the SM8350 camera NoC clock
 rates

Put the camera NoC's levels (300 and 400 MHz, the vendor driver's low
SVS and SVS ones) on the camnoc_axi branch, which the VFE sets from the
pixel clock, as on SM8550. On the RCG nothing set them, and the clock
stayed at the 19.2 MHz the camera clock controller starts with: the VFE
then received frames (start and end of frame on its RDI) but never
completed a reg update or a buffer, with a CCIF violation on the RDI's
write master.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c | 30 +++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

